@page "/docs/common/responsive"

@* Responsive values: breakpoint maps, the rule for what's responsive, hiding by width, fluid
   text, and form columns that follow the form's width. From docs/styling.md. *@

<ArticlePage Section="common" Slug="responsive">
    <Lead>
        A style prop that changes with screen size accepts one value, or one value per breakpoint. The server writes
        classes and CSS variables only for the breakpoints you set, so a page fits a phone with JavaScript off too.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">One value per breakpoint</Heading>
        <Code Block Language="razor">@Maps</Code>
        <Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Breakpoint</th><th>From</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>Base</code></td><td>0, every screen</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>Sm</code></td><td>640px</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>Md</code></td><td>768px</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>Lg</code></td><td>1024px</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>Xl</code></td><td>1280px</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </Prose>
        <TextBlock>
            Each value applies from its breakpoint up, until a larger breakpoint replaces it. Only the values you set
            produce CSS, so <Code>new() { Md = 6 }</Code> keeps the component's own value below 768px.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">What's responsive</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Parameters for values that change with screen size accept a map: direction, gap, spacing, columns, sizes and
            alignment. Switches don't. <Code>Grow</Code>, <Code>Shrink</Code>, <Code>Wrap</Code>, <Code>Inline</Code> and
            the rest are plain booleans, so you can write them bare, as in <Code>&lt;Row Wrap&gt;</Code>. Each component's
            API page marks its responsive parameters.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Hide or show by width</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            To hide a component from a breakpoint up, set <Code>HiddenFrom</Code>. To show it only from a breakpoint up,
            set <Code>VisibleFrom</Code>. Nearly every component has both, fields included:
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor">@Hidden</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">Fluid text</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Fluid text grows smoothly with the screen instead of in steps. To make a
            <Anchor Href="docs/components/heading">Heading</Anchor> or <Anchor Href="docs/components/text-block">TextBlock</Anchor>
            fluid, set <Code>MinSize</Code>. The text is <Code>MinSize</Code> on a 360px screen and <Code>Size</Code> at
            1280px.
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor">@Fluid</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">Sized by the container</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            A <Anchor Href="docs/components/form">Form</Anchor> or <Anchor Href="docs/components/fieldset">Fieldset</Anchor>
            with <Code>Columns</Code> set to a plain number follows its own width, not the screen's. So the same form fits
            a page, a dialog and a drawer with no breakpoints. A <Anchor Href="docs/components/grid">Grid</Anchor> with
            <Code>MinChildWidth</Code> fits as many columns as there's room for.
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor">@Container</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">Next steps</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/common/style-props">Style props</Anchor>: every prop that accepts a map.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/common/forms">Forms and validation</Anchor>: columns in a form.</ListItem>
        </List>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private const string Maps = """
        <Stack Gap="4">...</Stack>
        <Stack Gap="new() { Base = 2, Md = 6 }">...</Stack>
        <Stack Direction="new() { Base = Direction.Column, Md = Direction.Row }">...</Stack>
        <Grid Columns="new() { Base = 1, Sm = 2, Lg = 4 }">...</Grid>
        """;

    private const string Hidden = """
        <Button HiddenFrom="Breakpoint.Md" StartIcon="Lucide.Menu">Menu</Button>
        <NavMenu VisibleFrom="Breakpoint.Md">...</NavMenu>
        """;

    private const string Fluid = """
        <Heading Size="TextSize.Xl5" MinSize="TextSize.Xl3">Ship on Friday</Heading>
        """;

    private const string Container = """
        <Form Model="Model" FormName="contact" Columns="2">...</Form>   @* two columns from 32rem of form *@
        <Grid MinChildWidth="Length.Rem(15)" Gap="4">...</Grid>
        """;
}
